From: Julian Decker <git@deckerjulian.com>
Subject: drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: check for a CEC adapter in the HPD work

repo_hpd_event() looked at hdmi->cec_adap->devnode without a test. The
pointer is set by the dw-hdmi-cec driver when it probes, so a hot-plug
event that comes first, or a board without that device, is a NULL pointer
fault.

The notification only matters to a registered adapter, so skip it while
there is none.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -448,7 +448,7 @@
 			if (hdmi->plat_data->set_ddc_io)
 				hdmi->plat_data->set_ddc_io(data, hdmi->hpd_state);
 #if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DRM_DW_HDMI_CEC)
-			if (hdmi->cec_adap->devnode.registered)
+			if (hdmi->cec_adap && hdmi->cec_adap->devnode.registered)
 				cec_queue_pin_hpd_event(hdmi->cec_adap,
 							hdmi->hpd_state,
 							ktime_get());
